class Solution {
    public void nextPermutation(int[] nums) {
        int n = nums.length;
        int ind = -1;

        // Step 1: find breakpoint
        for(int i = n - 2; i >= 0; i--){
            if(nums[i] < nums[i+1]){
                ind = i;
                break;
            }
        }

        // Step 2: if no breakpoint
        if(ind == -1){
            reverse(nums, 0, n-1);
            return;
        }

        // Step 3: swap with next greater element
        for(int i = n - 1; i > ind; i--){
            if(nums[i] > nums[ind]){
                int temp = nums[i];
                nums[i] = nums[ind];
                nums[ind] = temp;
                break;
            }
        }

        // Step 4: reverse remaining part
        reverse(nums, ind + 1, n - 1);
    }

    // Reverse function
    public void reverse(int[] nums, int start, int end){
        while(start < end){
            int temp = nums[start];
            nums[start] = nums[end];
            nums[end] = temp;
            start++;
            end--;
        }
    }
}




For Next Permutation, always remember this 4-step pattern:

1️⃣ Find breakpoint (nums[i] < nums[i+1])
2️⃣ Find next greater element from right
3️⃣ Swap
4️⃣ Reverse the right half

Time Complexity: O(n)
Space Complexity: O(1)
